WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.128 --> 00:00:01.440
(intriguing music)

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.660
- [Presenter] Tensions
over Taiwan have soared.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.850
A visit from House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.620
and comments from other US officials

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.104
about the island have infuriated China.

00:00:10.104 --> 00:00:14.021
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.260
The self-ruled island has
grown into a durable democracy

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.720
and major semiconductor producer.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.810
The US has promised to
help it defend itself.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.120
- [Reporter] Are you willing
to get involved militarily

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.520
to defend Taiwan if it comes to that?

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.420
- Yes.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.500
- [Presenter] But the problem is,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.750
China sees it as part of its own territory

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.880
and has threatened to
seize it if necessary.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.100
- Over the past year, the Chinese military

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.900
has also sent dozens of planes,
bombers and fighter jets

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.883
into the air space close to Taiwan.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.550
- [Presenter] So as Taiwan is perhaps

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.310
the most explosive issue
in US-China relations,

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.533
here's how we got here and what's next.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.040
The first thing to know is that Taiwan,

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.720
which is located off China's coast,

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.210
has been self-governed since 1949.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.000
That's when the Communist Party
took power in mainland China

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.730
and some nationalists fled to the island.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.320
- For China, Taiwan is seen

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.050
as always been the one that got away.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.700
When the Chinese Communist Party

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.130
first founded the People's
Republic of China,

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.640
Taiwan was never a part
of the People's Republic.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.730
Instead it was governed
by the Kuomintang Party

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:24.510
that had fled to the island
after brutal civil war.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.240
Ever since then, every
Chinese leader has sought

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.940
to reunify Taiwan with the mainland.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.830
- [Presenter] And that
includes President Xi Jinping

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.380
who has made bringing Taiwan
under mainland control

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.054
a key goal of his legacy.

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:39.971
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.310
But the US has shown support
for President Tsai Ing-wen.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.200
From Beijing's perspective, she's a leader

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.831
who is dangerously pushing
Taiwan closer to independence.

00:01:52.831 --> 00:01:54.870
(grandiose music)
(camera shutter clicking)

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.810
Taiwan became a bigger
bilateral issue between the US

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.840
and China during the
administration of President Trump.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.150
- What president Donald
Trump did was to make it

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.270
part of US policy to
tighten ties with Taiwan

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.450
and this has continued
under President Biden.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.550
- [Presenter] For decades,
the US has sent weapons

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.140
and more recently, has sent troops

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.203
to provide military training
despite China's warnings.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.320
The US has a few reasons to do that.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.650
- Firstly, it's the US'
ninth largest trading partner

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.920
and Taiwan is also a key
part of global supply chains.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.860
Taiwan is also a litmus
test for US credibility

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.020
in the region, because the US allies

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.320
will watch US' treatment
of Taiwan carefully.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.370
- [Presenter] One reason Taiwan

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.320
is so strategic for the US and China

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.450
is the role it plays in manufacturing.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.000
It's home to the world's
most critical chip-maker

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.950
and semiconductors have
been in short supply

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.093
over the past year.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.700
So what's next?

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.830
China has made a series
of moves in the region

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.650
in what Taiwan sees as attempts
to discourage the island

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.040
from forging closer ties
with the US and other allies.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.770
- What we've seen is a PLA unit posting

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.840
on a social media account the video

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.060
of a recent military drill that happened

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.280
off the coast of
southeastern Fujian province

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.900
and facing Taiwan.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.037
The caption of the video read,

00:03:09.037 --> 00:03:11.730
"We're ready to fight any time."

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.140
- [Presenter] China
also said it would hold

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.800
live fire military drills
around Taiwan in early August,

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.110
but this doesn't mean China
will actually invade the island,

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.020
which carries a lot of risk
considering Washington's pledges

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.694
to help Taiwan defend itself.

00:03:24.694 --> 00:03:25.980
(intriguing music)

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.020
Taiwan is one of a number of issues

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.240
such as trade and
technology that have soured

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.640
US-China relations in recent years.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.470
Despite the risks of escalation,

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.690
the US is signaling that
even with war raging

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.880
in Ukraine, it can remain very active

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.010
in the strategic Asia-Pacific region.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.660
- If the US doesn't stand up

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.630
for Taiwan in the face of China coercion,

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.720
then US credibility in the region suffers

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.400
and it would affect its relationship

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.263
with other allies in the region.

